    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Triage a shared Gmail inbox with Claude and create tasks in Asana and Slack\n\nOperations teams and assistants who sort a shared inbox by hand and lose requests in the pile.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: Polls the mailbox every minute for new messages via Gmail or Microsoft Outlook triggers; threads are handled as a unit.\n1. Receive and de-duplicate\n2. Classify\n3. Fetch context\n4. Extract tasks and dates\n5. Draft routine replies\n6. Route\n7. Approve and send\n8. Daily digest\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Gmail / Outlook, Asana / Linear / Notion, Slack.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nEdit the categories and the routing rules in the Config node; replace Asana with Linear or Notion.\nGuardrail to keep: Drafts require approval by default; auto-send is enabled per category by the inbox owner and logged.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/email-triage-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
